: '/etc/reboot -- the documented name, and the truth about it.'
: ''
: '	/etc/reboot [-p]'
: ''
: 'THE COMMODORE 900 CANNOT RESTART ITSELF IN SOFTWARE, so this halts and'
: 'says so instead of pretending.  The evidence, since the Lexicon page for'
: 'reboot(1) shipped with this system describes a machine that can:'
: ''
: '  - There is no reset port.  The boot ROM is fixed read-only at physical'
: '    0 and there is no overlay or bank register to switch it back in;'
: '    nothing in the ROM I/O map is a reset line.'
: '  - Z8001 reset is a pin event, not an instruction.  It also resets the'
: '    Z8010 MMU and the peripherals, which a jump into the ROM would not,'
: '    so the ROM would start with the running system MMU mapping in force.'
: '  - The one restart interface the ROM declares -- rom_restart in struct'
: '    romconf -- is never assigned.  The ROM fills in rom_bram, rom_eram'
: '    and rom_ctype and leaves the rest zero, so calling it would jump to'
: '    segment 0 offset 0.'
: '  - The 3.x /etc/reboot this replaces was never a candidate: its'
: '    reboot() is an 8042 keyboard-controller pulse-reset (etc-3.x'
: '    ATrebootas.s), PC/AT hardware this machine does not have.  The 4.x'
: '    one calls a kernel cohcall(COH_REBOOT) that this kernel has no'
: '    syscall for.'
: ''
: 'For an orderly shutdown use /etc/shutdown, which warns the users first.'
: 'This is the single-user shortcut and it unmounts nothing that is busy --'
: '/etc/halt reports what it could not detach and syncs it anyway.'
: ''
: 'This shell has no comment lexer, so the explanation is in : arguments.'

if /bin/test "$1" = -p
then
	echo 'This machine cannot restart itself; it will halt instead.'
	echo -n 'Press Enter to halt, or interrupt to stay up: '
	read answer
fi
echo 'reboot: this machine cannot restart itself in software.'
echo 'reboot: halting instead -- press reset to restart.'
exec /etc/halt
